    {
      "name": "15 · Runbooks",
      "description": "Composite scenarios. Read the description of each request for the sequence to follow.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Full canary rollout — verify traffic split",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{gateway_base_url}}/api/v1/users/me", "host": ["{{gateway_base_url}}"], "path": ["api","v1","users","me"] }
          },
          "description": "Reset canary counters (in folder 12), then run THIS request 100 times via Runner. Expected split: ~95 v1, ~5 v2 (matches Weight=95:5 in application.yml). Grafana 'Canary rollout' row should reflect the same.\n\nBonus: change weight to 75:25 in application.yml, restart, re-run — split should shift accordingly."
        },
        {
          "name": "Trigger + verify a fallback (bulkhead saturation)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{gateway_base_url}}/api/v1/users/me", "host": ["{{gateway_base_url}}"], "path": ["api","v1","users","me"] }
          },
          "description": "1. Add Thread.sleep(3000) to a v1 user-service endpoint. Restart.\n2. Run THIS request 30 times in parallel via Postman Runner (Delay: 0, iterations: 30).\n3. Expected: ~15 slow 200s (bulkhead=15), rest fast 503 with X-Fallback-Reason: bulkhead-full.\n4. Verify in Grafana → Bulkhead saturation reaches 1.0 briefly.\n\nRemove the sleep + restart to reset."
        },
        {
          "name": "Idempotency race — same key, parallel requests",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Idempotency-Key", "value": "race-{{$timestamp}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\"item\":\"race\",\"qty\":1}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{gateway_base_url}}/api/v1/orders", "host": ["{{gateway_base_url}}"], "path": ["api","v1","orders"] }
          },
          "description": "Run 5x in parallel via Postman Runner (Iterations: 5, Delay: 0). NOTE: {{$timestamp}} generates ONE value at each iteration, so use a static value instead to trigger the race.\n\nExpected: 1 x 201 (first wins the Redis lock), 4 x 409 Conflict (duplicate_request_in_flight).\n\nVerify: Grafana → Idempotency outcomes shows conflict counter climbing."
        }
      ]
    }
